% IF and COND are one construct: condition/result pairs and a default.

### name: cond.if.three-argument
--- dialect
mariadb
--- bindings
{"N": {"kind": "column", "column": "n", "type": "NUM"}}
--- source
IF(N > 0, "yes", "no")
--- expect
CASE WHEN (`n` > 0) THEN 'yes' ELSE 'no' END
===
### name: cond.if.two-argument-defaults-to-empty-text
--- note
spec §7.2: the two-argument form yields TEXT "" when the condition is false.
--- dialect
mariadb
--- bindings
{"N": {"kind": "column", "column": "n", "type": "NUM"}}
--- source
IF(N > 0, "yes")
--- expect
CASE WHEN (`n` > 0) THEN 'yes' ELSE '' END
===
### name: cond.cond.ladder
--- dialect
mariadb
--- bindings
{"S": {"kind": "column", "column": "score", "type": "NUM"}}
--- source
COND(S >= 90, "A", S >= 80, "B", "F")
--- expect
CASE WHEN (`score` >= 90) THEN 'A' WHEN (`score` >= 80) THEN 'B' ELSE 'F' END
===
### name: cond.kind.unifies-when-the-branches-agree
--- note
Both branches are TEXT, so the CASE is TEXT — and asCondition() refuses it,
which is the point of tracking the kind at all.
--- dialect
mariadb
--- as
condition
--- source
IF(TRUE, "a", "b")
--- error
E_SQL_SHAPE
===
### name: cond.kind.bool-branches-make-a-condition
--- dialect
mariadb
--- as
condition
--- bindings
{"N": {"kind": "column", "column": "n", "type": "NUM"}}
--- source
IF(N > 0, N > 10, FALSE)
--- expect
CASE WHEN (`n` > 0) THEN (`n` > 10) ELSE FALSE END
===
### name: cond.refuse.condition-must-be-bool
--- dialect
mariadb
--- source
IF("yes", 1, 2)
--- error
E_SQL_SHAPE 1:4
===
### name: cond.refuse.constant-condition-mismatch-is-at-the-if
--- note
The translator never folds, so `IF(TRUE, "x", 1)` is still the IF when its two
kinds are refused, at 1:1. That is also the column run() reports E_NOT_NUM at
for the same source (ctl.if.constant-condition-result-keeps-the-if-position):
one node, one column, in both lanes -- pinned because the in-memory optimiser
once hoisted the literal and moved run()'s answer to 1:10.
--- dialect
mariadb
--- source
IF(TRUE, "x", 1) >= 1
--- error
E_SQL_SHAPE 1:1
===
### name: cond.nested
--- dialect
mariadb
--- bindings
{"N": {"kind": "column", "column": "n", "type": "NUM"}}
--- source
IF(N > 0, IF(N > 10, "big", "small"), "none")
--- expect
CASE WHEN (`n` > 0) THEN CASE WHEN (`n` > 10) THEN 'big' ELSE 'small' END ELSE 'none' END
